579
00:52:13,839 --> 00:52:17,634
<i>Here are some of the many things
we don't know about heptapods.</i>

580
00:52:17,718 --> 00:52:21,096
<i>Greek. Hepta, "Seven. "Pod, "Foot."</i>

581
00:52:21,180 --> 00:52:23,557
<i>"Seven feet." Heptapod.</i>

582
00:52:25,184 --> 00:52:26,602
<i>Who are they?</i>

583
00:52:27,936 --> 00:52:30,355
<i>Trying to answer this
in any meaningful way</i>

584
00:52:30,439 --> 00:52:32,065
<i>is hampered by the fact that,</i>

585
00:52:32,149 --> 00:52:34,526
<i>outside being able
to see them and hear them,</i>

586
00:52:34,610 --> 00:52:37,738
<i>the heptapods leave
absolutely no footprint.</i>

587
00:52:39,615 --> 00:52:42,784
<i>The chemical composition
of their spaceship is unknown.</i>

588
00:52:42,868 --> 00:52:46,913
<i>The shell emits no waste,
no gas, no radiation.</i>

589
00:52:46,997 --> 00:52:49,707
<i>Assuming that the shells
communicate with each other,</i>

590
00:52:49,791 --> 00:52:51,293
<i>they do so without detection.</i>

591
00:52:51,960 --> 00:52:56,632
<i>The air between the shells is untroubled
by sonic emission or light wave.</i>

592
00:52:58,550 --> 00:53:01,261
<i>Are they scientists or tourists?</i>

593
00:53:01,345 --> 00:53:04,723
<i>If they're scientists, they don't seem
to ask a lot of questions.</i>

594
00:53:07,726 --> 00:53:09,645
<i>Why did they park where they did?</i>

595
00:53:10,395 --> 00:53:13,398
<i>The world's most decorated experts
can't crack that one.</i>

596
00:53:13,899 --> 00:53:17,068
<i>The most plausible theory is that
they chose places on Earth</i>

597
00:53:17,152 --> 00:53:20,113
