598
00:53:20,197 --> 00:53:21,739
<i>But there are exceptions.</i>

599
00:53:21,823 --> 00:53:25,326
<i>The next most plausible theory is that
Sheena Easton had a hit song</i>

600
00:53:25,410 --> 00:53:28,664
<i>at each of these sites in 1980.
So, we just don't know.</i>

601
00:53:31,583 --> 00:53:33,543
<i>How do they communicate?</i>

602
00:53:34,127 --> 00:53:36,630
<i>Here, Louise is putting us all to shame.</i>

603
00:53:37,214 --> 00:53:40,884
<i>The first breakthrough was to discover
that there's no correlation</i>

604
00:53:40,968 --> 00:53:44,179
<i>between what a heptapod says
and what a heptapod writes.</i>

605
00:54:00,237 --> 00:54:04,949
<i>Unlike all written human languages,
their writing is semasiographic.</i>

606
00:54:05,033 --> 00:54:08,370
<i>It conveys meaning.
It doesn't represent sound.</i>

607
00:54:13,458 --> 00:54:17,462
<i>Perhaps they view our form of writing
as a wasted opportunity,</i>

608
00:54:17,713 --> 00:54:19,923
<i>passing up a second
communications channel.</i>

609
00:54:25,721 --> 00:54:27,305
<i>We have our friends in Pakistan</i>

610
00:54:27,389 --> 00:54:31,559
<i>to thank for their study
of how heptapods write.</i>

611
00:54:31,643 --> 00:54:35,814
<i>Because, unlike speech,
a logogram is free of time.</i>

612
00:54:38,483 --> 00:54:40,985
<i>Like their ship or their bodies,</i>

613
00:54:41,069 --> 00:54:44,239
<i>their written language has
no forward or backward direction.</i>

614
00:54:44,906 --> 00:54:48,076
<i>Linguists call this
"nonlinear orthography,"</i>

615
00:54:48,160 --> 00:54:51,580
<i>which raises the question,
"Is this how they think?"</i>

616
00:54:53,749 --> 00:54:56,376
<i>Imagine you wanted to
write a sentence using two hands,</i>

617
00:54:56,460 --> 00:54:58,211
<i>starting from either side.</i>

618
00:54:59,171 --> 00:55:01,881
<i>You would have to know
each word you wanted to use</i>

619
00:55:01,965 --> 00:55:04,885
<i>as well as
how much space that it would occupy.</i>

620
00:55:06,762 --> 00:55:08,846
<i>A heptapod can write a complex sentence</i>

621
00:55:08,930 --> 00:55:11,057
<i>in two seconds, effortlessly.</i>

622
00:55:11,141 --> 00:55:13,852
<i>It's taken us a month to make
the simplest reply.</i>

623
00:55:14,603 --> 00:55:17,355
<i>Next, expanding vocabulary.</i>

624
00:55:17,439 --> 00:55:20,889
