01:01:54,586 --> 01:01:57,797
Yeah. It affects how you see everything.
It was...

711
01:01:58,673 --> 01:02:00,216
I'm curious,

712
01:02:00,300 --> 01:02:02,469
are you dreaming in their language?

713
01:02:12,520 --> 01:02:15,148
I may have had a few dreams,
but I don't...

714
01:02:16,858 --> 01:02:20,445
I don't think that
that makes me unfit to do this job.

715
01:02:39,881 --> 01:02:40,882
Did you sleep?

716
01:02:41,633 --> 01:02:42,759
A little.

717
01:02:43,551 --> 01:02:44,803
Do you know Mandarin?

718
01:02:49,098 --> 01:02:50,642
It is shifting.

719
01:02:57,565 --> 01:02:59,065
The voice you're about to hear

720
01:02:59,484 --> 01:03:01,694
belongs to China's military chief,

721
01:03:03,530 --> 01:03:04,906
General Shang.

722
01:03:05,907 --> 01:03:07,242
Pull it up.

723
01:03:10,203 --> 01:03:12,204
We got a satellite feed here
of who he's talking to,

724
01:03:12,288 --> 01:03:13,790
if you want to look.

725
01:03:14,874 --> 01:03:16,125
Wait, go back.

726
01:03:17,877 --> 01:03:19,212
Stop.

727
01:03:21,214 --> 01:03:25,093
He's saying that each of the 12
is offering advanced technology.

728
01:03:27,595 --> 01:03:29,848
And back again. And play.

729
01:03:33,351 --> 01:03:37,313
"Our science team is attempting
to decode the sets."

730
01:03:38,022 --> 01:03:40,024
"Sets." I don't know what that means.

731
01:03:40,733 --> 01:03:42,401
Something about advantage.

732
01:03:42,485 --> 01:03:44,946
"Suits, honor, and flowers."

733
01:03:45,280 --> 01:03:46,447
I don't...

734
01:03:47,949 --> 01:03:49,700
I don't know, that's all.

735
01:03:49,784 --> 01:03:51,994
I don't know what it means either.

736
01:03:52,078 --> 01:03:54,789
An hour ago, China mobilized forces.

737
01:03:54,873 --> 01:03:56,791
And now, Russia is following suit.

738
01:03:57,458 --> 01:03:59,210
Shang's about to start something.

739
01:03:59,752 --> 01:04:01,713
Following suit, "suits."

740
01:04:03,882 --> 01:04:06,425
Suits. Honor. Flowers.

741
01:04:06,509 --> 01:04:09,178
Colonel, those are all
tile sets in mahjong.

742
01:04:11,055 --> 01:04:12,432
God, are they...

743
01:04:13,016 --> 01:04:16,019
Are they using a game
to converse with their heptapods?

744
01:04:17,770 --> 01:04:19,438
Maybe. Why?

745
01:04:19,522 --> 01:04:23,317
Well, let's say that I taught them chess
instead of English.

746
01:04:23,401 --> 01:04:25,194
Every conversation would be a game,

747
01:04:25,278 --> 01:04:28,572
every idea expressed
through opposition, victory, defeat.

748
01:04:28,656 --> 01:04:29,782
You see the problem?

749
01:04:31,200 --> 01:04:34,161
If all I ever gave you was a hammer...

750
01:04:34,245 --> 01:04:35,663
Everything's a nail.

751
01:04:37,707 --> 01:04:39,709
We need to ask the big question.

752
01:04:41,044 --> 01:04:42,295
Ready or not.

753
01:04:46,674 --> 01:04:47,675
Right, so...

754
01:04:47,759 --> 01:04:50,159
Okay, let me know
what temperature you use, okay?

755
01:04:51,054 --> 01:04:53,681
No, this is the same as before.

756
01:04:54,223 --> 01:04:55,308
- See.
- I...

757
01:04:55,892 --> 01:04:57,742
Yeah, no, but between three and four.

758
01:04:59,395 --> 01:05:00,980
- All right, time to go.
- Okay.

759
01:05:12,075 --> 01:05:14,994
<i>Ninety-six minutes remaining
in the session. Over.</i>

760
01:05:23,711 --> 01:05:24,796
Okay.

761
01:05:28,967 --> 01:05:30,051
Heptapod's purpose.

762
01:05:41,729 --> 01:05:44,357
Heptapod purpose. Earth.
What is your purpose?

763
01:05:51,906 --> 01:05:53,156
Do we only have Costello?

764
01:05:58,538 --> 01:06:00,289
Okay. There you are.

765
01:06:22,603 --> 01:06:23,896
What does it say?

766
01:06:32,739 --> 01:06:34,282
"Offer weapon."

767
01:06:37,481 --> 01:06:39,077
But you saw what they wrote.

768
01:06:39,161 --> 01:06:40,287
But you saw what they wrote.

769
01:06:40,371 --> 01:06:41,705
Using a word they don't fully understand.

770
01:06:41,789 --> 01:06:43,207
- It could be just a request.
- Or a warning.

771
01:06:43,291 --> 01:06:44,292
Enough!

772
01:06:44,876 --> 01:06:45,918
Louise?

773
01:06:46,627 --> 01:06:48,629
We don't know if they understand

774
01:06:48,713 --> 01:06:51,174
the difference between
a weapon and a tool.

775
01:06:51,883 --> 01:06:53,801
Our language, like our culture, is messy,

776
01:06:53,885 --> 01:06:55,469
and sometimes one can be both.

777
01:06:55,553 --> 01:06:59,181
I think it's quite possible that they're
asking us to offer them something,

778
01:06:59,265 --> 01:07:02,518
not the other way around,
like the first part of a trade.

779
01:07:02,643 --> 01:07:05,938
So, how do we clarify their intentions
beyond those two words?

780
01:07:06,022 --> 01:07:07,398
Well, I go back in.

781
01:07:07,482 --> 01:07:09,566
Right away, we go back in
and we clear this up.

782
01:07:09,650 --> 01:07:10,734
It's more complicated than that.

783
01:07:10,818 --> 01:07:12,668
How is it more complicated than that?

784
01:07:13,905 --> 01:07:17,241
Colonel, the Secretary of Defense
is on the line for you.

785
01:07:24,373 --> 01:07:27,793
We need to sit on this information
till we know what it means.

786
01:07:27,877 --> 01:07:29,378
So, we aren't sharing it
with our enemies.

787
01:07:29,462 --> 01:07:30,754
We have to consider the idea

788
01:07:30,838 --> 01:07:32,965
that our visitors are prodding us
to fight among ourselves

789
01:07:33,049 --> 01:07:35,342
until only one faction prevails.

790
01:07:35,426 --> 01:07:36,593
There's no evidence of that.

791
01:07:36,677 --> 01:07:38,053
Sure there is.

792
01:07:38,137 --> 01:07:39,972
Just grab a history book.

793
01:07:40,306 --> 01:07:42,934
The British with India,
the Germans with Rwanda.

794
01:07:44,018 --> 01:07:46,145
They even got a name for it in Hungary.

795
01:07:51,192 --> 01:07:52,276
Yeah.

796
01:07:52,985 --> 01:07:55,612
We're a world with no single leader.

797
01:07:55,696 --> 01:07:58,240
It's impossible to deal with
just one of us.

798
01:07:58,324 --> 01:07:59,974
And with the word "weapon" now...

799
01:08:00,785 --> 01:08:02,036
Halpern.

800
01:08:03,204 --> 01:08:04,330
Yes, sir.

801
01:08:18,845 --> 01:08:21,638
Copy that. Waiting for instructions.

802
01:08:21,722 --> 01:08:23,474
No confirmation yet.

803
01:08:23,558 --> 01:08:24,934
Standing by.

804
01:08:25,309 --> 01:08:26,435
Anything?

805
01:08:27,937 --> 01:08:29,272
What did they say?

806
01:08:30,231 --> 01:08:32,775
China and Russia are off the grid.
They aren't speaking to anyone.

807
01:08:32,859 --> 01:08:36,404
Whatever they learned
in their last session has them spooked.

808
01:08:38,573 --> 01:08:39,740
Yes, sir.

809
01:08:40,241 --> 01:08:41,658
We have orders to do the same.

810
01:08:41,742 --> 01:08:42,951
Wait, these are our allies.

811
01:08:43,035 --> 01:08:44,119
Colonel, you can't shut us down.

812
01:08:44,203 --> 01:08:45,913
- Put us on radio silence.
- Do it.

813
01:08:46,372 --> 01:08:48,707
We received a message from the...

814
01:08:48,791 --> 01:08:50,126
Damn it!

815
01:08:50,877 --> 01:08:52,127
We need to be talking to each other.

816
01:08:52,211 --> 01:08:54,755
You wanna talk to them?
Find out what this means.

817
01:09:00,344 --> 01:09:02,138
<i>Base-camp talk is now offline.</i>

818
01:09:02,597 --> 01:09:05,099
<i>- All interpreters...</i>
- No confirmation. They're offline.

819
01:09:05,183 --> 01:09:08,186
<i>...stand down
and report to unit coordinators.</i>

820
01:09:10,313 --> 01:09:12,314
We've never re-entered a session before.

821
01:09:12,398 --> 01:09:15,025
Look, Louise, trust me, okay?
We've got time.

822
01:09:15,109 --> 01:09:17,059
We've just gotta step on it, all right?

823
01:09:17,945 --> 01:09:19,280
<i>"Use weapon."</i>

824
01:09:19,780 --> 01:09:20,989
<i>This is the alien message</i>

825
01:09:21,073 --> 01:09:22,950
<i>said to have provoked
the Chinese government</i>

826
01:09:23,034 --> 01:09:26,704
<i>to withdraw their scientists
from the international mission today.</i>

827
01:09:27,288 --> 01:09:29,623
<i>In a statement, General Shang said,</i>

828
01:09:29,707 --> 01:09:33,085
<i>"China no longer trusts the aliens
who want to divide us."</i>

829
01:09:33,169 --> 01:09:34,670
<i>"Humanity must be protected."</i>

830
01:09:35,338 --> 01:09:38,341
<i>China has asked for immediate talks
at the UN.</i>

831
01:09:41,510 --> 01:09:44,138
<i>Alpha one-niner, this is Condor. Over.</i>

832
01:09:48,684 --> 01:09:51,311
<i>Alpha one-niner, this is Condor.</i>

833
01:09:51,395 --> 01:09:52,897
<i>Come in. Over.</i>

834
01:09:57,818 --> 01:09:59,403
<i>Captain Marks, Condor.</i>

835
01:09:59,487 --> 01:10:02,657
<i>Not receiving transmission.
Squelch twice if you hear mine.</i>

836
01:10:04,033 --> 01:10:07,333
<i>Captain Marks, all escort groups
are ordered to cease all activity.</i>

837
01:10:38,276 --> 01:10:40,360
No, no, no.
Dr. Banks, you can't go in there.

838
01:10:40,444 --> 01:10:41,778
We just need to ask one question.

839
01:10:41,862 --> 01:10:45,157
Dr. Banks, the session is finished.
You can't...

840
01:10:45,366 --> 01:10:46,742
You can't go back in. It's dangerous.

841
01:10:46,826 --> 01:10:48,493
Look, we just need five minutes.
Don't sweat it.

842
01:10:48,577 --> 01:10:50,538
Marks, let them go.

843
01:10:53,499 --> 01:10:55,126
Hey, Abbott.

844
01:11:00,381 --> 01:11:03,301
So, what are we calling this, session 37?

845
01:11:03,759 --> 01:11:05,386
No, 36, part two.

846
01:11:05,553 --> 01:11:06,637
Okay.

847
01:11:07,054 --> 01:11:08,180
Yeah.

848
01:11:13,936 --> 01:11:15,020
Why are they on their own?

849
01:11:15,104 --> 01:11:17,064
We've been attempting
to hail Captain Marks.

850
01:11:17,148 --> 01:11:18,982
The escort units are not responding, sir.

851
01:11:19,066 --> 01:11:20,067
Why not?

852
01:11:21,402 --> 01:11:22,695
Send security.

853
01:11:25,990 --> 01:11:29,410
"Offer weapon. Question mark."

854
01:11:34,373 --> 01:11:36,584
Are you offering us something?

855
01:11:45,718 --> 01:11:48,262
"Technology. Apparatus. Method"?

856
01:11:48,721 --> 01:11:50,847
Yeah, see, this is a different word.

857
01:11:50,931 --> 01:11:53,392
This segment, it's a lot busier.

858
01:11:59,106 --> 01:12:00,274
"Give."

859
01:12:01,192 --> 01:12:02,568
"Technology."

860
01:12:04,153 --> 01:12:05,237
"Now."

861
01:12:13,996 --> 01:12:15,623
What's he doing?

862
01:12:21,170 --> 01:12:22,755
<i>Captain, on your 10.</i>

863
01:12:26,133 --> 01:12:28,802
<i>Mutineers are to be apprehended
without engaging.</i>

864
01:12:28,886 --> 01:12:31,680
<i>We don't want to risk
antagonizing our visitors. Over.</i>

865
01:12:32,473 --> 01:12:35,642
<i>Security detail inbound, sir.
T-minus four minutes remaining.</i>

866
01:12:35,726 --> 01:12:37,311
<i>We need to see this through.</i>

867
01:12:37,520 --> 01:12:39,062
<i>Okay, this is it. Lock and load.</i>

868
01:12:39,146 --> 01:12:41,064
<i>We just need to hold them off
until it's done.</i>

869
01:12:41,148 --> 01:12:43,650
<i>Copy that.
Warning shots as explicit fire only.</i>

870
01:12:43,734 --> 01:12:44,985
<i>Load up and get to cover.</i>

871
01:12:45,069 --> 01:12:47,019
<i>Stay fresh and we can avoid casualties.</i>

872
01:13:14,098 --> 01:13:16,684
Abbott wants me to write on the barrier.

873
01:13:21,522 --> 01:13:22,982
Can you even do that?

874
01:13:24,567 --> 01:13:26,026
I don't know.

875
01:13:42,293 --> 01:13:43,836
I can't do it with both hands.

876
01:14:55,908 --> 01:14:56,909
Louise.

877
01:15:12,299 --> 01:15:13,300
What is that?

878
01:15:13,384 --> 01:15:16,095
- Free fire!
- Over there! I'm hit! I'm hit!

879
01:15:59,221 --> 01:16:01,806
Hey, hey, hey. Take it easy.

880
01:16:01,890 --> 01:16:03,391
You suffered a concussion.

881
01:16:03,475 --> 01:16:04,977
Just lay back.

882
01:16:07,688 --> 01:16:09,273
How are you feeling?

883
01:16:17,948 --> 01:16:19,324
How is Ian?

884
01:16:19,408 --> 01:16:21,327
Same as you. He's okay.

885
01:16:22,995 --> 01:16:24,163
Who...

886
01:16:24,580 --> 01:16:26,081
Who did this?

887
01:16:26,415 --> 01:16:29,168
Some soldiers.
Been watching too much TV.

888
01:16:33,005 --> 01:16:34,464
What is that?

889
01:16:34,548 --> 01:16:36,591
Now, take it easy. Take it easy.

890
01:16:36,675 --> 01:16:38,426
The site's no longer secure.

891
01:16:38,510 --> 01:16:40,054
We're standing by to evacuate.

892
01:16:40,387 --> 01:16:41,639
Where's Ian?

893
01:16:42,973 --> 01:16:45,809
Weber came and got him
maybe 10 minutes ago.

894
01:16:45,893 --> 01:16:48,854
But he wouldn't leave
until he knew you were okay.

895
01:16:51,398 --> 01:16:52,983
The whole tent is on the clock

896
01:16:53,067 --> 01:16:55,736
to figure out whatever it is
you were given up there.

897
01:17:01,992 --> 01:17:03,661
This is all of it.

898
01:17:04,078 --> 01:17:06,278
The feed wasn't interrupted
by the explosion?

899
01:17:07,039 --> 01:17:09,083
Not as far as we can see.

900
01:17:10,751 --> 01:17:12,335
You see something?

901
01:17:12,419 --> 01:17:13,670
I don't know yet.

902
01:17:13,754 --> 01:17:16,631
I'm gonna need my team
to get together with Louise's team.

903
01:17:16,715 --> 01:17:18,008
I need everybody working on this.

904
01:17:18,092 --> 01:17:19,093
We cannot leave.

905
01:17:19,968 --> 01:17:21,177
Glad to see you're awake.

906
01:17:21,261 --> 01:17:24,014
We need to go back in and we need
to explain to them this wasn't our fault.

907
01:17:24,098 --> 01:17:26,266
- We can't go back inside.
- We have to tell them... We have to.

908
01:17:26,350 --> 01:17:28,310
What happened in there was an attack.

909
01:17:28,394 --> 01:17:31,354
We can hope for the best, but
I have orders to prepare for retaliation.

910
01:17:31,438 --> 01:17:32,689
We may have to evacuate.

911
01:17:32,773 --> 01:17:36,610
No, that's the wrong move.
As long as they stay, we have to stay.

912
01:18:10,436 --> 01:18:12,604
Well, they're not leaving.

913
01:18:14,189 --> 01:18:16,442
Why does this feel worse?

914
01:18:20,988 --> 01:18:22,739
<i>China is on the offensive.</i>

915
01:18:22,823 --> 01:18:24,240
<i>They're positioning their military</i>

916
01:18:24,324 --> 01:18:26,242
<i>to blow the alien vessel
right out of the sky.</i>

917
01:18:26,326 --> 01:18:27,577
<i>And if this happens,</i>

918
01:18:27,661 --> 01:18:32,332
<i>we can't sit around waiting
for retaliation, so get prepared.</i>

919
01:18:32,416 --> 01:18:34,459
<i>The Air Force and infantry
are standing by.</i>

920
01:18:34,543 --> 01:18:35,544
Yes, sir.

921
01:18:37,337 --> 01:18:40,715
<i>Tonight, China becomes
the first world power</i>

922
01:18:40,799 --> 01:18:42,885
<i>to declare war against the aliens.</i>

923
01:18:43,677 --> 01:18:47,180
<i>Following the failure of
diplomatic efforts at the United Nations,</i>

924
01:18:47,264 --> 01:18:50,642
<i>China has confirmed that
its language experts have, tonight,</i>

925
01:18:50,726 --> 01:18:53,770
<i>delivered an ultimatum
at the Shanghai site.</i>

926
01:18:53,854 --> 01:18:55,939
<i>In a televised statement, General Shang,</i>

927
01:18:56,023 --> 01:18:58,191
<i>Chairman of the People's Liberation Army,</i>

928
01:18:58,275 --> 01:19:01,945
<i>said the aliens have 24 hours
to leave Chinese territory</i>

929
01:19:02,029 --> 01:19:03,697
<i>or face destruction.</i>

930
01:19:03,781 --> 01:19:06,991
<i>And he urged all other world leaders
to unite with China</i>

931
01:19:07,075 --> 01:19:09,619
<i>and take a similar stance.</i>

932
01:19:09,703 --> 01:19:13,039
<i>With a huge buildup of forces
at their landing sites,</i>

933
01:19:13,123 --> 01:19:18,170
<i>Pakistan, Russia, and Sudan are
thought to be following China's lead.</i>

934
01:19:33,769 --> 01:19:35,729
It can't be random.

935
01:19:51,203 --> 01:19:53,247
It's going to take us years.

936
01:19:58,335 --> 01:20:00,212
<i>What's this term here?</i>

937
01:20:04,216 --> 01:20:05,592
<i>Mom.</i>

938
01:20:07,594 --> 01:20:08,679
Mom.

939
01:20:10,180 --> 01:20:11,347
Sweetie?

940
01:20:11,431 --> 01:20:13,808
What's this term for that thing like a...

941
01:20:13,892 --> 01:20:15,102
Like a technical term?

942
01:20:15,894 --> 01:20:19,189
Where we make a deal and
we both get something out of it?

943
01:20:19,273 --> 01:20:20,815
"Compromise."

944
01:20:20,899 --> 01:20:22,025
No.

945
01:20:22,693 --> 01:20:27,573
Like, it's a competition,
but both sides end up happy.

946
01:20:29,074 --> 01:20:30,325
Like a win-win.

947
01:20:31,118 --> 01:20:32,619
More science-y than that.

948
01:20:33,328 --> 01:20:35,622
If you want science, call your father.

949
01:20:50,262 --> 01:20:51,597
Thank you.

950
01:21:02,274 --> 01:21:03,609
Sorry.

951
01:21:04,026 --> 01:21:06,445
It's okay. I'm up.

952
01:21:11,408 --> 01:21:13,035
What time is it?

953
01:21:14,328 --> 01:21:17,414
It's time you open that bottle
you've been hiding.

954
01:21:21,001 --> 01:21:23,294
You cracked something, didn't you?

955
01:21:23,378 --> 01:21:24,588
Yeah, come here.

956
01:21:26,757 --> 01:21:28,175
Take a look at this section.

957
01:21:28,675 --> 01:21:30,677
It seems to be talking about time.

958
01:21:30,761 --> 01:21:34,138
Their symbol for "time" is everywhere.

959
01:21:34,222 --> 01:21:35,849
So, what is this?

960
01:21:36,850 --> 01:21:39,853
A formula for faster-than-light travel?

961
01:21:39,937 --> 01:21:41,355
Who can tell?

962
01:21:42,230 --> 01:21:43,690
There are too many gaps.

963
01:21:43,774 --> 01:21:45,025
Nothing's complete.

964
01:21:45,359 --> 01:21:46,734
Then it dawned on me.

965
01:21:46,818 --> 01:21:48,195
Come here.

966
01:21:50,030 --> 01:21:51,198
Right here.

967
01:21:52,449 --> 01:21:55,368
Stop focusing on the ones,
look at the zeroes.

968
01:21:55,452 --> 01:21:58,705
How much of this is data?
How much of it is negative space?

969
01:22:00,123 --> 01:22:01,917
So, I measured it.

970
01:22:03,669 --> 01:22:05,337
0.0833 recurring.

971
01:22:11,969 --> 01:22:14,262
Perhaps you'd like that as a fraction.

972
01:22:17,557 --> 01:22:19,393
One of 12.

973
01:22:22,479 --> 01:22:25,440
What they're saying right here
is that this is one of 12.

974
01:22:25,816 --> 01:22:27,692
We are part of a larger whole.

975
01:22:27,776 --> 01:22:29,527
Or we're one of 12 contestants
for the prize.

976
01:22:29,611 --> 01:22:30,778
Why do I have to talk to him?

977
01:22:30,862 --> 01:22:32,488
We're all working together here.

978
01:22:32,572 --> 01:22:34,282
We need to talk to the other sites.

979
01:22:34,366 --> 01:22:36,951
We need to help them with what they've
gotten from the other heptapods.

980
01:22:37,035 --> 01:22:38,870
In case you don't remember,
we're blacked out.

981
01:22:38,954 --> 01:22:41,748
China just threatened to destroy
their shell. We're on our own.

982
01:22:41,832 --> 01:22:43,625
Yeah, but this says that
all of the pieces fit together.

983
01:22:43,709 --> 01:22:46,128
And I'm telling you
that no one else cares.

984
01:22:46,586 --> 01:22:49,631
Two hours ago, we pulled this audio
off a secure channel in Russia.

985
01:22:49,715 --> 01:22:52,676
Someone on the science team there
was broadcasting wide.

986
01:22:54,886 --> 01:22:59,349
<i>In their final session, the alien said,
"There is no time.</i>"

987
01:22:59,433 --> 01:23:01,684
<i>"Many become one."</i>

988
01:23:01,768 --> 01:23:03,668
<i>I feel we have all been given weapons.</i>

989
01:23:04,104 --> 01:23:07,232
<i>If anyone is receiving this, please...</i>

990
01:23:13,613 --> 01:23:15,657
Well, I mean,

991
01:23:15,866 --> 01:23:18,743
there are a lot of ways
you can interpret what he's saying.

992
01:23:18,827 --> 01:23:20,870
I don't need an interpreter
to know what this means.

993
01:23:20,954 --> 01:23:22,914
Russia just executed
one of their own experts

994
01:23:22,998 --> 01:23:24,291
to keep their secrets.

995
01:23:24,458 --> 01:23:27,001
"Many become one" could
just be their way of saying,

996
01:23:27,085 --> 01:23:28,711
"Some assembly required."

997
01:23:28,795 --> 01:23:30,755
Why hand it out to us in pieces?

998
01:23:30,839 --> 01:23:32,340
Why not just give it all over?

999
01:23:32,424 --> 01:23:35,093
Well, what better way to force us
to work together for once?

1000
01:23:35,177 --> 01:23:36,803
Even if I did believe you,

1001
01:23:36,887 --> 01:23:39,389
how in the world you gonna get
anybody else to play along

1002
01:23:39,473 --> 01:23:40,849
or give up their data?

1003
01:23:42,017 --> 01:23:43,977
We offer ours in return.

1004
01:23:44,686 --> 01:23:45,728
Yeah?

1005
01:23:45,812 --> 01:23:47,397
What, trade?

1006
01:23:47,481 --> 01:23:48,815
It's a non-zero sum game.

1007
01:23:51,568 --> 01:23:52,986
"Non-zero sum game."

1008
01:23:55,113 --> 01:23:56,364
That's it.

1009
01:23:56,448 --> 01:23:58,200
Yeah, thanks.

1010
01:24:05,373 --> 01:24:09,043
Nine of the landing sites
have gone total comms blackout.

1011
01:24:09,127 --> 01:24:11,629
Only way to reach them
is to physically drive there and yell

1012
01:24:11,713 --> 01:24:14,340
at the border guards, which we're doing,
but it won't be fast enough.

1013
01:24:14,424 --> 01:24:16,926
There's got to be a way to...
To get the message to them.

1014
01:24:17,010 --> 01:24:19,929
To our allies maybe, but at this stage,
it's too little too late.

1015
01:24:20,013 --> 01:24:22,849
<i>What we need is to get
all the other nations online</i>

1016
01:24:22,933 --> 01:24:24,684
<i>before one starts global war,</i>

1017
01:24:24,768 --> 01:24:26,811
<i>and there's no way for us to reach them.</i>

1018
01:24:26,895 --> 01:24:28,396
Wait. Hold on a second.

1019
01:24:28,480 --> 01:24:29,689
There is.

1020
01:24:30,565 --> 01:24:32,359
<i>It's right above us.</i>

1021
01:24:33,026 --> 01:24:34,826
<i>That's problematic for us right now.</i>

1022
01:24:35,278 --> 01:24:38,072
The Pentagon's convinced
our shell will retaliate.

1023
01:24:38,156 --> 01:24:41,326
My guess is they'll order us
to evacuate within the hour.

1024
01:24:41,660 --> 01:24:43,161
Look, they're not our enemy.

1025
01:24:43,245 --> 01:24:44,954
They've made
no act of aggression towards us.

1026
01:24:45,038 --> 01:24:46,998
Maybe this is
their way of being aggressive.

1027
01:24:47,082 --> 01:24:49,000
That's not the question.

1028
01:24:49,084 --> 01:24:51,128
Well, what is the question?

1029
01:24:51,628 --> 01:24:54,756
How do we get you back in that room
when it's half a mile straight up?

1030
01:24:54,840 --> 01:24:56,383
I think our work here is done.

1031
01:24:57,300 --> 01:24:59,845
It's in the hands of our superiors now.

1032
01:25:20,240 --> 01:25:22,242
What the hell is she doing?

1033
01:26:15,337 --> 01:26:19,007
No. God. Oh, God. No.

1034
01:28:38,897 --> 01:28:40,148
Costello?

1035
01:28:43,151 --> 01:28:44,694
Where's Abbott?

1036
01:28:54,537 --> 01:28:57,499
Abbott is death process

1037
01:29:14,307 --> 01:29:15,683
I'm sorry.

1038
01:29:18,353 --> 01:29:20,146
We're sorry.

1039
01:29:24,025 --> 01:29:25,652
I need you to...

1040
01:29:26,986 --> 01:29:30,240
I need you to send a message
to the other sites.

1041
01:29:36,955 --> 01:29:40,125
Louise has weapon

1042
01:29:48,174 --> 01:29:49,759
Use weapon

1043
01:29:49,843 --> 01:29:51,010
I don't...

1044
01:29:51,678 --> 01:29:53,179
I don't understand.

1045
01:29:53,847 --> 01:29:56,891
What is your purpose here?

1046
01:30:04,190 --> 01:30:08,570
We help humanity

1047
01:30:12,699 --> 01:30:16,995
In three thousand years

1048
01:30:18,288 --> 01:30:21,666
we need humanity help

1049
01:30:24,002 --> 01:30:26,129
How can you know the future?

1050
01:30:43,062 --> 01:30:44,397
I don't...

1051
01:30:45,815 --> 01:30:47,233
I don't understand.

1052
01:30:48,151 --> 01:30:50,320
Who is this child?

1053
01:30:55,158 --> 01:30:58,453
The show is called
<i>Mommy and Daddy Talk to Animals.</i>

1054
01:31:10,924 --> 01:31:14,427
Louise sees future

1055
01:31:24,687 --> 01:31:28,483
Weapon opens time

1056
01:31:32,904 --> 01:31:34,072
Wait.

1057
01:31:34,197 --> 01:31:36,282
No... Wait!

1058
01:32:25,331 --> 01:32:26,957
- Dr. Banks!
- Louise!

1059
01:32:27,041 --> 01:32:28,710
Are you all right?

1060
01:32:31,045 --> 01:32:33,547
- Hey. You all right?
- Yeah.

1061
01:32:33,631 --> 01:32:35,299
- Here, come on. What happened?
- I'm fine.

1062
01:32:35,383 --> 01:32:37,134
Tried to figure it out. This is too big.

1063
01:32:37,218 --> 01:32:40,012
Doesn't matter now.
We have orders to evacuate.

1064
01:32:40,096 --> 01:32:43,891
- Why?
- Russia and Sudan are following China.

1065
01:32:45,351 --> 01:32:47,478
Ian. I don't understand why the...

1066
01:32:47,562 --> 01:32:48,771
<i>Help me, Mama.</i>

1067
01:32:50,023 --> 01:32:51,232
<i>Louise?</i>

1068
01:32:51,316 --> 01:32:52,525
Oh, my God.

1069
01:32:52,609 --> 01:32:53,985
Mom.

1070
01:32:56,904 --> 01:32:58,364
Mama!

1071
01:33:00,450 --> 01:33:01,909
Sorry, honey.

1072
01:33:05,413 --> 01:33:07,748
What day is it? Do you know, baby?

1073
01:33:07,832 --> 01:33:09,083
Sunday.

1074
01:33:14,756 --> 01:33:17,258
Are you gonna leave me like Daddy did?

1075
01:33:18,718 --> 01:33:21,637
Hannah, honey,
your daddy didn't leave you.

1076
01:33:21,721 --> 01:33:24,182
You're gonna see him this weekend.

1077
01:33:25,058 --> 01:33:27,727
He doesn't look at me
the same way anymore.

1078
01:33:36,194 --> 01:33:37,862
That's my fault.

1079
01:33:40,156 --> 01:33:43,076
I told him something
that he wasn't ready to hear.

1080
01:33:45,244 --> 01:33:46,412
What?

1081
01:33:50,667 --> 01:33:53,002
Well, believe it or not,

1082
01:33:53,086 --> 01:33:55,713
I know something that's going to happen.

1083
01:33:57,882 --> 01:34:00,593
I can't explain how I know. I just do.

1084
01:34:02,095 --> 01:34:05,098
And when I told your daddy,
he got really mad.

1085
01:34:07,058 --> 01:34:09,811
And he said I made the wrong choice.

1086
01:34:12,230 --> 01:34:14,607
What? What's going to happen?

1087
01:34:17,860 --> 01:34:21,447
It has to do with a really rare disease.

1088
01:34:24,784 --> 01:34:26,619
And it's unstoppable.

1089
01:34:28,913 --> 01:34:30,748
Kind of like you are.

1090
01:34:31,332 --> 01:34:34,710
Your swimming, and your poetry,

1091
01:34:34,794 --> 01:34:38,047
and all the other amazing things
that you share with the world.

1092
01:34:38,631 --> 01:34:40,466
I am unstoppable?

1093
01:34:41,300 --> 01:34:42,593
Yeah.

1094
01:34:59,485 --> 01:35:00,820
I got you.

1095
01:35:02,655 --> 01:35:04,073
Louise?

1096
01:35:04,824 --> 01:35:06,242
Louise.

1097
01:35:07,577 --> 01:35:10,245
I just realized why my husband left me.

1098
01:35:10,329 --> 01:35:11,830
My husband left me.

1099
01:35:11,914 --> 01:35:13,749
You were married?

1100
01:35:13,833 --> 01:35:16,169
Come on. Let's get out of here.

1101
01:35:50,787 --> 01:35:51,954
Mama?

1102
01:35:52,038 --> 01:35:53,164
Yeah?

1103
01:35:53,664 --> 01:35:55,792
Why is my name Hannah?

1104
01:35:56,542 --> 01:35:57,960
Yeah, got it right here.

1105
01:35:58,044 --> 01:35:59,879
Get those people back, please.

1106
01:36:00,838 --> 01:36:05,926
Well, your name is very special
because it is a palindrome.

1107
01:36:06,010 --> 01:36:09,305
It reads the same forward and backward.

1108
01:36:09,722 --> 01:36:12,225
- All right, guys, give me a hand here.
- Yes, sir.

1109
01:36:12,975 --> 01:36:15,311
That goes in the back.

1110
01:36:28,950 --> 01:36:31,493
<i>Civilian contractors must have their
authorization badges</i>

1111
01:36:31,577 --> 01:36:33,079
<i>and passkeys when checking...</i>

1112
01:36:40,253 --> 01:36:42,713
<i>Evacuation underway...</i>

1113
01:36:46,175 --> 01:36:47,301
<i>Hey.</i>

1114
01:36:47,969 --> 01:36:50,095
Look, we're done here.

1115
01:36:50,179 --> 01:36:51,479
We're taking this with us.

1116
01:37:16,455 --> 01:37:17,957
I can read it.

1117
01:37:22,086 --> 01:37:23,921
- I know what it is.
- What?

1118
01:37:24,005 --> 01:37:26,048
It's not a weapon, it's a gift.

1119
01:37:26,883 --> 01:37:28,634
The weapon is their language.

1120
01:37:28,718 --> 01:37:31,094
They gave it all to us.
Do you understand what that means?

1121
01:37:31,178 --> 01:37:33,847
So we can learn Heptapod, if we survive.

1122
01:37:33,931 --> 01:37:36,809
If you learn it, when you really learn it,

1123
01:37:36,893 --> 01:37:39,243
you begin to perceive time
the way that they do.

1124
01:37:39,395 --> 01:37:42,022
So you can see what's to come.

1125
01:37:42,106 --> 01:37:44,275
But time, it isn't the same for them.

1126
01:37:44,650 --> 01:37:46,611
- It's non-linear.
- Look.

1127
01:37:46,944 --> 01:37:49,238
We did our best, but it wasn't enough.

1128
01:37:50,531 --> 01:37:52,157
The captain will load you up.

1129
01:37:52,241 --> 01:37:53,991
You're lifting off in five minutes.

1130
01:37:54,201 --> 01:37:57,830
Ian, Louise,
it was an honor to work with ya.

1131
01:37:58,873 --> 01:38:00,291
Good luck.

1132
01:38:03,628 --> 01:38:05,004
Hey, Colonel!

1133
01:38:12,094 --> 01:38:13,944
I'm gonna find out where we're going.

1134
01:38:21,771 --> 01:38:24,190
Wake up, Mommy.

1135
01:38:59,642 --> 01:39:01,185
Dr. Banks.

1136
01:39:02,395 --> 01:39:03,729
A pleasure.

1137
01:39:04,355 --> 01:39:05,480
General Shang.

1138
01:39:05,564 --> 01:39:07,108
The pleasure is mine, really.

1139
01:39:08,067 --> 01:39:10,110
Your President said

1140
01:39:10,194 --> 01:39:13,447
he was honored to host me
at the celebration...

1141
01:39:13,531 --> 01:39:15,533
- Yes.
- ...but I confess,

1142
01:39:16,367 --> 01:39:19,078
the only reason why I'm here is to

1143
01:39:20,538 --> 01:39:22,498
meet you in person.

1144
01:39:23,499 --> 01:39:25,835
Me? Well, I'm flattered. Thank you.

1145
01:39:26,919 --> 01:39:29,254
Now, 18 months ago,

1146
01:39:29,338 --> 01:39:31,424
you did something remarkable.

1147
01:39:32,049 --> 01:39:35,511
Something not even my superior has done.

1148
01:39:37,388 --> 01:39:38,972
And what's that?

1149
01:39:39,056 --> 01:39:40,975
You changed my mind.

1150
01:39:43,185 --> 01:39:46,856
You're the reason for this unification.

1151
01:39:47,732 --> 01:39:51,527
All because you reached out to me
on my private number.

1152
01:39:53,612 --> 01:39:54,613
Your private number.

1153
01:39:54,697 --> 01:39:57,283
General, I don't know
your private number.

1154
01:40:04,582 --> 01:40:06,292
Now you know.

1155
01:40:08,461 --> 01:40:10,921
I do not claim to know
how your mind works,

1156
01:40:12,590 --> 01:40:16,177
but I believe it was important for you
to see that.

1157
01:40:17,636 --> 01:40:19,138
I called you, didn't I?

1158
01:40:20,598 --> 01:40:22,767
Yes, you did.

1159
01:40:33,986 --> 01:40:35,112
Louise.

1160
01:40:51,670 --> 01:40:54,173
- All right, let's shut down the system.
- Sir.

1161
01:40:55,508 --> 01:40:57,885
There's a sat-line here dialing China.

1162
01:41:00,262 --> 01:41:01,762
Here? What do you mean "here"?

1163
01:41:04,141 --> 01:41:05,601
Come on, come on.

1164
01:41:06,894 --> 01:41:08,437
Whose phone is it?

1165
01:41:12,566 --> 01:41:13,734
It's your phone, sir.

1166
01:41:21,408 --> 01:41:22,701
Search base camp now.

1167
01:41:23,202 --> 01:41:25,037
Find out who's using that phone.

1168
01:41:25,579 --> 01:41:27,998
- Hold on to those coordinates.
- Yes, sir.

1169
01:41:28,082 --> 01:41:30,584
Come on. What'd I say?

1170
01:41:31,544 --> 01:41:34,630
What'd I say? Come on.

1171
01:41:43,848 --> 01:41:45,224
Come on.

1172
01:41:46,392 --> 01:41:49,103
I will never forget what you said.

1173
01:41:59,738 --> 01:42:02,783
You told me my wife's dying words.

1174
01:42:20,509 --> 01:42:21,968
Found the source of the phone call.

1175
01:42:22,052 --> 01:42:24,452
It's in the clean room.
Waiting for instructions.

1176
01:42:26,765 --> 01:42:28,684
What are you doing?

1177
01:42:29,351 --> 01:42:31,186
- What are you doing?
- Changing someone's mind.

1178
01:42:31,270 --> 01:42:33,647
- Can you buy me 20 seconds?
- We don't have time for this right now.

1179
01:42:33,731 --> 01:42:35,315
No, trust me, buy me 20 seconds.
Do you trust me?

1180
01:42:35,399 --> 01:42:36,817
- Okay! Yeah.
- You trust me?

1181
01:42:40,154 --> 01:42:41,238
Dr. Banks!

1182
01:42:42,072 --> 01:42:43,699
Drop the phone now or we shoot!

1183
01:42:46,994 --> 01:42:49,413
- Drop it!
- Yeah. I'm sorry!

1184
01:42:51,957 --> 01:42:53,792
You're committing an act of treason!

1185
01:42:59,506 --> 01:43:00,966
- Yes.
- Drop it!

1186
01:43:01,133 --> 01:43:02,635
It's done. I'm done.

1187
01:43:18,067 --> 01:43:22,196
<i>Communications blackout from all 12
landing sites continues this evening.</i>

1188
01:43:23,280 --> 01:43:24,990
<i>Hold on, we are just hearing...</i>

1189
01:43:25,074 --> 01:43:26,074
<i>And I'm being told</i>

1190
01:43:26,158 --> 01:43:28,827
<i>we're going to cut this report
to tell you breaking news.</i>

1191
01:43:28,911 --> 01:43:31,580
<i>Breaking now, China has called
an emergency press conference.</i>

1192
01:43:31,664 --> 01:43:34,875
<i>General Shang, Commander-in-chief
of the People's Liberation Army,</i>

1193
01:43:34,959 --> 01:43:37,169
<i>has announced in
an emergency press conference</i>

1194
01:43:37,253 --> 01:43:38,962
<i>that China is standing down.</i>

1195
01:43:39,046 --> 01:43:42,007
<i>China is stating that
all intelligence they have received</i>

1196
01:43:42,091 --> 01:43:44,593
<i>will be shared immediately
with all the other landing sites.</i>

1197
01:43:44,677 --> 01:43:47,137
<i>Scientists from around the world
are sifting through information received</i>

1198
01:43:47,221 --> 01:43:48,555
<i>- from the UK, Japan...
- Breaking news,</i>

1199
01:43:48,639 --> 01:43:50,891
<i>the Russian armed forces are now
revealing the information</i>

1200
01:43:50,975 --> 01:43:53,226
<i>they've acquired from
both of their landing sites</i>

1201
01:43:53,310 --> 01:43:55,395
<i>and have declared the Black Sea
a demilitarized zone.</i>

1202
01:43:55,479 --> 01:43:59,029
<i>...one of the 12 pieces of this puzzle
that's being slowly put together.</i>

1203
01:45:47,508 --> 01:45:50,177
<i>So, Hannah.</i>

1204
01:45:51,387 --> 01:45:54,056
<i>This is where your story begins.</i>

1205
01:45:56,225 --> 01:45:58,102
<i>The day they departed.</i>

1206
01:46:02,189 --> 01:46:03,649
You all right?

1207
01:46:06,902 --> 01:46:11,115
<i>Despite knowing the journey
and where it leads...</i>

1208
01:46:14,451 --> 01:46:16,161
<i>I embrace it...</i>

1209
01:46:18,580 --> 01:46:22,000
<i>and I welcome every moment of it.</i>

1210
01:46:36,640 --> 01:46:41,145
- H-A-N-N-A-H.
- H-A-N-N-A-H.

1211
01:46:54,908 --> 01:47:00,246
- Now backward. H-A-N-N-A-H.
- A-N-N-A-H.

1212
